Start
/ list-query: one step, one query. Each stage is a goal; each behaviour a comment with the test that proves it.
/ The plang here says what is wanted; the coder rewrites each test in plang that compiles.
- call goal Stage1
- call goal Stage2
- call goal Stage3

Stage1
/ The type and the action: where with and/or, group, distinct, order; SQL order by default.
/ A where with two conditions joined by and keeps only what passes both
- call goal /module/list/query/WhereAnd
/ A where with or keeps what passes either
- call goal /module/list/query/WhereOr
/ A where value given as a %variable% is read when the step runs
- call goal /module/list/query/WhereVariable
/ Order by a field, ascending and descending
- call goal /module/list/query/OrderBy
/ Distinct drops repeated elements
- call goal /module/list/query/Distinct
/ Group by a field gives {key, items}; order by after it orders each group's items
- call goal /module/list/query/GroupThenOrder
/ The parts run in SQL order whatever order the step says them ("order by age, where age > 20" filters first)
- call goal /module/list/query/SqlOrder
/ With %!list.query.setting.execution% = written, the parts run in the order the step says them
- call goal /module/list/query/WrittenOrder
/ The input list is unchanged: the query answers a new list
- call goal /module/list/query/InputUnchanged
/ A field the elements don't have is an error naming the part ("where: no field 'agee'")
- call goal /module/list/query/UnknownField

Stage2
/ The builder picks list.query from the words.
/ "filter %users% where type is 'student' and age > 20, group by name, distinct, order by age" builds to one list.query with those parts
- call goal /module/list/query/build/ManyParts
/ "where %users% age > 20, write to %adults%" builds to a one-part query
- call goal /module/list/query/build/OnePart
/ "sort %people% by age" with no destination builds with an explicit write to %people%
- call goal /module/list/query/build/WriteBack

Stage3
/ The four are gone; their behaviours hold through list.query.
/ The two old where tests, rewritten as queries, pass: partial-field filters and a misspelled field
- call goal /module/list/query/PartialFieldFilters
- call goal /module/list/query/MisspelledFieldIsAnError
